Negative control for the scope catch-all every scenario route ends in.

Narrows `SCOPE_SUFFIX_SEGMENT` to a single dynamic segment, so a registered
route still serves `/useClientEmails/as/client` and stops matching the
`/for/:type/:id` retarget entirely. This is the silent shape the design's 4.2.2
probe warned about: the url still works, the actor still parses, and
`.for('client', id)` simply never arrives — FE-2824's failure mode arriving by
way of the router.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds (module lane, measured 2026-08-11 — `pnpm vitest run --project module`
from playgrounds/labs-nuxt). Baseline is 28/28 green, so all 10 failures below
are this mutant's:

  10 failed | 18 passed (28)

  scenario-routes.spec.ts (6)
    @G3d the directory IS the route — nothing else names one
      x ends every scenario path in the scope catch-all
    @G3d the four scope shapes still resolve (operator: NON-NEGOTIABLE)
      x serves the bare url, where the binding's own scope applies
      x serves /:page/as/:actor
      x serves /:brandId/:page/as/:actor
      x serves the full path — brand, actor and the .for() retarget together
      x keeps the retarget reachable with no brand in the url

  scenario-nav-routes.spec.ts (3)
    @G6 every derived link resolves against the registered routes
      x derives a link for the canary and excludes its handoff target (R8)
      x leaves no derived link unmatched by the router
    @G6 the sidebar entry is the composable's own NAME (D1)
      x links the very entry it labels, so the two cannot drift

  scenario-auth-collect.spec.ts (1)
    @G6 the overlay the funnel names is MOUNTED on that page (D2)
      x resolves it as a child of the page, so the page stays underneath

The blast radius is every guard that RESOLVES a scenario url — the nav lane's
derived links and the auth funnel's page-child overlay resolve through the same
registered paths, so narrowing the suffix reds them too.

The collision guard stays green (all four "@G3d amendment 2" cases pass), which
is the point: it only reads route NAMES, so narrowing the suffix is invisible
to it.

